---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, BASE, liveSocials } from '../site.config';

// Gaps only Arun can fill. Rendered in dev so they're impossible to miss; never shipped.
const isDev = import.meta.env.DEV;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description={`About ${SITE.author} — engineer, writer, chess player, perpetual starter of things.`}
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-head">
      <span class="hand">the longer version</span>
      <h1 class="page-head__title">Hi, I'm Arun.</h1>
      <p class="page-head__lede">
        I'm a software engineer who writes to understand and builds to find out.
        This page is the story behind both halves of this site.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="story">

      <section class="act">
        <p class="act__n">I.</p>
        <div class="act__body">
          <h2>The day job</h2>
          <p>
            For more than a decade I've built distributed systems &mdash; lately the
            unglamorous kind that move money: invoices, ledgers, the plumbing that has
            to be right every single time. It taught me to respect boring correctness,
            and to distrust anything that only works in the demo.
          </p>
          {isDev && <p class="todo">TODO (Arun): where it started &mdash; the first thing you built, or the moment you knew you'd be an engineer.</p>}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="act">
        <p class="act__n">II.</p>
        <div class="act__body">
          <h2>The musings</h2>
          <p>
            Since 2021 I've kept notes for my future self &mdash; on motivation, on
            salvaging bad days, on why wandering beats efficient lists. Most of them sat
            in a notebook for years before they came here. I publish them because
            they've held up.
          </p>
          <blockquote>
            Be 100% involved and experience everything. Good, bad and ugly. Live through
            it all and tell stories to help everyone who comes after you.
            <cite><a href={`${BASE}blog/nothing-is-final`}>Nothing is Final</a>, 2021</cite>
          </blockquote>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="act">
        <p class="act__n">III.</p>
        <div class="act__body">
          <h2>The madness</h2>
          <p>
            Some ideas won't leave me alone until I build them: a memory architecture
            aimed at ARC-AGI, a serious dessert map of Hyderabad, a Chrome extension
            that snaps half your tabs out of existence, a rebuild of the Government of
            India's global quiz. AI has changed what one curious person can make in a
            weekend &mdash; I intend to find out how far that goes.
          </p>
          <p><a href={`${BASE}projects`}>See everything I've built &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="act">
        <p class="act__n">IV.</p>
        <div class="act__body">
          <h2>Everything else</h2>
          <ul class="also">
            <li><strong>Chess</strong> &mdash; for the way it punishes the first idea that feels right.</li>
            <li><strong>Quizzing</strong> &mdash; the joy of knowing one strange fact at exactly the right moment.</li>
            <li><strong>Reading</strong> &mdash; science told as story (Labatut, Deutsch), and accounts of small teams doing impossible engineering.</li>
          </ul>
          {isDev && <p class="todo">TODO (Arun): one specific detail each &mdash; a favourite opening or game, a quiz you won or lost, the book that changed your mind.</p>}
          <p><a href={`${BASE}library`}>The library &rarr;</a></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="act act--chasing">
        <p class="act__n">V.</p>
        <div class="act__body">
          <h2>What I'm chasing</h2>
          <p>
            Money has never been a reliable reason for me to get up early. What works is
            seeing a better way for the world to exist &mdash; and patiently building
            toward it until it's obvious to everyone else. For me that points at science,
            at making hard things buildable, and at the places I come from getting better
            at making things.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

    </article>

    {liveSocials.length > 0 && (
      <p class="elsewhere">
        Find me elsewhere:{' '}
        {liveSocials.map((s, i) => (
          <>{i > 0 && ' · '}<a href={s.url} target="_blank" rel="me noopener noreferrer">{s.label}</a></>
        ))}
      </p>
    )}
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .story { max-width: 44rem; }

  .act {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3rem 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    padding-block: var(--space-8);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .act__n { font-style: italic; color: var(--accent); font-size: var(--size-xl); line-height: 1.2; }
  .act__body h2 { font-size: var(--size-2xl); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .act__body p { line-height: var(--lh-relaxed); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .act__body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .act--chasing h2 { font-style: italic; }

  blockquote {
    margin-block: var(--space-6);
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: var(--size-lg);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  cite {
    display: block;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    font-style: normal;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .also { list-style: none; margin-bottom: var(--space-4); }
  .also li { padding-block: var(--space-2); line-height: 1.6; }
  .also strong { font-weight: 500; }

  .todo {
    font-family: var(--hand);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: #b23a3a;
    background: #fff4d6;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
    transform: rotate(-0.5deg);
  }

  .elsewhere {
    max-width: none;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .act { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-1); }
  }
</style>
